@startuml mate_agent_service_responsibility_boundary
title HTTP Boundaries: Message SSE and Builtin JSON

' Source evidence (pi-mono-java 1f801dbb82bdda30478e3354e685e3153b179a0c):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeEventController.java.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventService.java.
' Observed behavior: the CampusClaw internal HTTP POST returns execution-scoped SSE without a public WebSocket path.
' Target-only design: the mate-service public HTTP contract and its SSE projection are not implemented in this repository.
' Architecture change: both hops use HTTP request-response, message responses stream SSE; Runtime Builtin commands return JSON.
' Product constraint: the UI receives chatId only; sessionId remains an internal Runtime identifier.
' Security hardening: mate-service terminates public auth and projects internal events instead of forwarding bytes transparently.
' Design reason: keep user-facing Chat lifecycle separate from durable Runtime Session identity and execution.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 18
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontColor #0F172A
skinparam ArrowColor #64748B
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #94A3B8
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam database {
  BorderColor #94A3B8
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  FontColor #334155
}

left to right direction

rectangle "Agent UI\n\nCall public HTTP operations\nUse chatId only\nRead execution-scoped SSE\nClose on stream end or error\nNever receive sessionId" as UI #EFF6FF

rectangle "mate-service\n\nOwn public HTTP and SSE\nAuthenticate the end user\nOwn Chat metadata and chatId\nMap public Chat ID to internal Session ID\nRun guardrails and orchestration\nCall CampusClaw with request credentials\nProject safe public events and errors" as Mate #FFF7ED

rectangle "CampusClaw\n\nOwn internal HTTP and SSE\nReceive request context without credential checks\nOwn Runtime Session and sessionId\nValidate Agent and Model\nBuild Context and execute Model and read tool\nPersist current-branch Entries\nOwn Steer, FollowUp, and Abort" as Runtime #ECFDF5

database "Mate Chat Store\n\nPublic Chat ID to internal Session ID\nProduct state (no Session name copy)\nUser ownership" as MateStore

database "RuntimeSessionStore\n\nSession state and configuration\nCurrent-branch Entries\nInternal execution state" as RuntimeStore

UI <--> Mate : public HTTP requests\nMessage JSON or scoped SSE\nPublic command protocol pending\nchatId scope
Mate <--> Runtime : internal HTTP requests\nResultBean, 204, or message SSE\nBuiltin command: JSON only\nsessionId scope
Mate --> MateStore : own and update
Runtime --> RuntimeStore : own and update

note bottom of Mate
The public and internal hops are independent contracts.
mate-service does not forward the internal stream byte for byte.
Public paths, VOs, errors, and event projection require
a separate operation-by-operation review.
end note

note bottom of Runtime
Each user-message POST owns one bounded SSE response.
Builtin commands return JSON; Skill execution is deferred.
Steer and FollowUp are separate HTTP requests that enqueue
into the active execution. Abort is another HTTP request.
The Runtime does not read chatId or end-user identity.
end note
@enduml
